  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#script-processing-start\r\n\r\nStep 9 currently says:\r\n\r\n> 9. If the element is flagged as \"parser\\-inserted\", but the element's node document is not the Document of the parser that created the element, then abort these steps\\.\r\n\r\nHowever Step 2 would have cleared the element's flag if it was set.\r\n\r\n> 2. If the element has its \"parser-inserted\" flag set, then set was-parser-inserted to true and unset the element's \"parser-inserted\" flag. Otherwise, set was-parser-inserted to false.\r\n\r\nPerhaps Step 9 should be checking the `was-parser-inserted` state instead of the element's flag? It doesn't look like any of the intermediate steps (3-8) could have changed the element's flag.",
